quran[21]{c,v,t}:
  26,207,then that (respite) which they enjoyed would not avail them.
  26,208,"We have never destroyed any town without having (sent) warners to it,"
  26,209,as a reminder (from Us). And We were never unjust.
  26,210,And the devils have not descended with it (i.e. the Qur’an).
  26,211,"Neither is it befitting for them, nor are they capable (of it)."
  26,212,"Indeed, they are strictly barred from (even) hearing (it)."
  26,213,"So do not invoke another god along with Allah, lest you should be among the punished."
  26,214,And warn the nearest of your kinsfolk.
  26,215,And lower your wing (of kindness) to the believers who follow you.
  26,216,"But if they disobey you, say: ‘I am absolved of what you do.’"
  26,217,"And put your trust in the All-Mighty, the All-Merciful,"
  26,218,"Who sees you when you stand (for prayer),"
  26,219,and your moving over and over among those who prostrate themselves (before Allah).
  26,220,"Indeed, He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing."
  26,221,Shall I inform you upon whom the devils descend?
  26,222,"They descend upon every sinful liar,"
  26,223,"who readily lends an ear (to Satanic whispers), and most of them are liars (when passing on information to people)."
  26,224,"As for the poets, only the deviants follow them."
  26,225,Have you not seen that they wander in every valley (of imagination)?
  26,226,And that they say what they do not do?
  26,227,"Except for those (poets) who believe, perform righteous deeds, remember Allah abundantly and defend themselves (by inspiring zeal and courage) after they were oppressed. And the wrongdoers will soon know to what evil end they will return."
